{%- comment -%}
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Totterful / Hankie Pals — Meet the maker
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A founder intro: portrait on the left inside two organic blobs, pull quote
  and bio on the right.

  The two blob paths are one authored shape each, on a 0..100 grid, generated
  from per-direction radii rather than hand-tuned bezier handles. Each path is
  used twice from a single source: the visible outline draws it in an SVG with
  viewBox="0 0 100 100", and the photo crop feeds the same string to a
  <clipPath clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox"> whose <path> carries
  transform="scale(0.01)". One string, two consumers, so the crop and the
  outline can never drift apart.

  preserveAspectRatio="none" on the outline is deliberate: objectBoundingBox
  normalises to the element's box, and "none" is the only setting that
  stretches the same way. The stroke stays exactly 2px at any size through
  vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" rather than a width divided by the scale.

  Transforms are split across nested elements wherever two things animate the
  same element, because the last animation to apply wins outright and would
  silently drop the other:
    back blob   — entrance scale on .hp-mm__back, idle wobble on its inner svg
    sticker     — entrance rotate+scale on .hp-mm__sticker, hover wiggle and
                  lift on the .hp-mm__pill inside it
    photo       — entrance fade+rise on .hp-mm__photo, hover zoom on its <img>
  Nesting them costs one wrapper each and removes the specificity fight
  entirely, which is what bit the solution-tabs reveal (README, "A reveal that
  takes itself away").

  The stickers hang outside the portrait cluster by design. overflow-x: clip on
  the section root is what keeps that from reaching the page as a horizontal
  scrollbar; it is `clip` rather than `hidden` so no scroll container is
  created. Below 990px the right-hand presets also move inboard, because a
  percentage that clears the cluster on a desktop does not clear a phone.

  No webfonts are loaded here. Every other section in this theme defers to
  Dawn's --font-heading-family / --font-body-family with a named fallback
  stack, and a section that fetched its own would ship a render-blocking
  request per instance. The signature face is its own property so it can be
  pointed at whatever the theme actually loads.

  Free text going into the inline style attribute is escaped. The signature
  font stack contains double quotes, and unescaped they close style="" early:
  every custom property declared after it silently vanishes, which first shows
  up as some unrelated padding resolving to zero.

  No script beyond the reveal. Sizes are px: Dawn's root font-size is 62.5%,
  so rem renders at 62.5% of its intended value. Every setting carries a
  `| default:`, because a setting added after a section was saved comes back
  nil on that saved instance.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  # Authored on a 0..100 grid. See scripts/gen-blob-paths.py for the generator
  # and the measured gap between the two.
  assign back_d = 'M 50.00 2.00 C 60.25 1.88, 72.95 10.89, 81.11 18.89 C 89.28 26.89, 98.76 39.39, 99.00 50.00 C 99.24 60.61, 90.69 74.69, 82.53 82.53 C 74.36 90.36, 61.31 96.53, 50.00 97.00 C 38.69 97.47, 22.73 93.19, 14.64 85.36 C 6.56 77.52, 0.68 60.96, 1.50 50.00 C 2.32 39.04, 11.51 27.59, 19.59 19.59 C 27.68 11.59, 39.75 2.12, 50.00 2.00 Z'
  assign photo_d = 'M 50.00 3.00 C 61.37 2.94, 76.96 7.87, 84.29 15.71 C 91.63 23.54, 93.94 38.51, 94.00 50.00 C 94.06 61.49, 91.98 77.15, 84.65 84.65 C 77.31 92.15, 60.84 95.71, 50.00 95.00 C 39.16 94.29, 27.51 87.91, 19.59 80.41 C 11.68 72.91, 3.09 60.72, 2.50 50.00 C 1.91 39.28, 8.14 23.89, 16.06 16.06 C 23.98 8.23, 38.63 3.06, 50.00 3.00 Z'

  assign sig_name = s.signature_name | default: 'Niku'

  # The portrait is the one image here, so its alt text is the one that has to
  # say something. The signature name is the fallback because "photo of Niku"
  # is still worth more to a screen reader than an empty string.
  assign portrait_alt = s.portrait_alt | default: ''
  if portrait_alt == blank
    assign portrait_alt = sig_name
  endif

  # `| default:` replaces false as well as nil, so a checkbox guarded with it
  # could never be switched off. Compared against false instead.
  assign animate = true
  if s.animate == false
    assign animate = false
  endif

  # Hoisted out of the image_tag call: a `| default:` written inline as a
  # filter argument binds to everything left of it, which is the whole tag.
  assign portrait_loading = s.portrait_loading | default: 'lazy'

  assign clip_id = 'hp-mm-clip-' | append: section.id
-%}

{% style %}
  .hp-mm {
    /* The section keeps its own layering to itself. Without this its
       positioned children are ordered against every other section on the
       page, and a sticker here can paint over a section further down. */
    isolation: isolate;
    /* The stickers overhang the portrait cluster on purpose. This stops that
       overhang from becoming a horizontal scrollbar on the page. `clip`
       rather than `hidden`: no scroll container, nothing to focus-scroll. */
    overflow-x: clip;

    --hp-mm-display: var(--font-heading-family, Bitter, "Chubbo", Georgia, serif);
    --hp-mm-body: var(--font-body-family, Lexend, "Quicksand", ui-rounded, system-ui, sans-serif);

    background: var(--hp-mm-bg);
    padding-block: var(--hp-mm-pt) var(--hp-mm-pb);
    /* The side gutter belongs to the section, not to the row. Dawn sets
       box-sizing: border-box globally, so padding on the row would come out
       of its 1116px and leave the text column 48px short of 540. */
    padding-inline: 24px;
  }

  .hp-mm__row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 480px minmax(0, 540px);
    gap: 96px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    max-width: 1116px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  /* --- Portrait cluster ---------------------------------------------------
     A square box the two blobs are measured against. Both children fill it by
     percentage, so the whole cluster scales from one width. */
  .hp-mm__portrait {
    position: relative;
    width: 480px;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    justify-self: center;
  }

  .hp-mm__back {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .hp-mm__back svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  /* 420 of the cluster's 480, inset 30 on every side — expressed as a share so
     the inset survives the mobile scale. */
  .hp-mm__photo {
    position: absolute;
    left: 6.25%;
    top: 6.25%;
    width: 87.5%;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    z-index: 2;
    background: var(--hp-mm-placeholder);
    clip-path: url(#{{ clip_id }});
    /* The crop lives here rather than on the <img> so the hover zoom inside
       it is still clipped, and so the entrance and the zoom are not two
       animations fighting over one element's transform. */
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hp-mm__photo img,
  .hp-mm__photo svg.placeholder-svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    transition: transform 500ms ease;
  }

  /* The outline traces the same path the crop uses. Stretched, not fitted:
     objectBoundingBox normalises to the box, and "none" is the only
     preserveAspectRatio that does the same. */
  .hp-mm__outline {
    position: absolute;
    left: 6.25%;
    top: 6.25%;
    width: 87.5%;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    z-index: 3;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hp-mm__outline svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    overflow: visible;
  }

  /* --- Stickers ----------------------------------------------------------- */
  .hp-mm__sticker {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 4;
    /* The tilt lives on this element; the pill inside carries the hover. */
    transform: rotate(var(--hp-mm-rot, 0deg));
    transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  }

  .hp-mm__pill {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    border: 2px solid var(--hp-mm-ink);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--hp-mm-sticker-bg, #FFFFFF);
    font-family: var(--hp-mm-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--hp-mm-ink);
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: transform 250ms ease;
  }

  .hp-mm__pill::before {
    content: "";
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--hp-mm-accent);
    flex: none;
  }

  .hp-mm__sticker--tr { left: 66.7%; top: 12.5%; }
  .hp-mm__sticker--bl { left: -2.1%; top: 79.2%; }
  .hp-mm__sticker--tl { left: -2.1%; top: 12.5%; }
  .hp-mm__sticker--br { left: 66.7%; top: 79.2%; }

  /* --- Text column -------------------------------------------------------- */
  .hp-mm__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 24px;
  }

  .hp-mm__eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--hp-mm-eyebrow-bg);
    font-family: var(--hp-mm-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 10px;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--hp-mm-ink);
  }

  .hp-mm__eyebrow::before {
    content: "";
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--hp-mm-accent);
    flex: none;
  }

  .hp-mm__quote {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--hp-mm-display);
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 36px;
    line-height: 46px;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    color: var(--hp-mm-ink);
  }

  .hp-mm__quote p { margin: 0; }

  .hp-mm__bio {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 520px;
    font-family: var(--hp-mm-body);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 27px;
    color: var(--hp-mm-muted);
  }

  .hp-mm__sig { margin: 0; }

  .hp-mm__sig-name {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--hp-mm-signature);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 34px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--hp-mm-accent);
  }

  .hp-mm__sig-title {
    display: block;
    margin-block-start: 4px;
    font-family: var(--hp-mm-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--hp-mm-ink);
  }

  /* --- Entrance -----------------------------------------------------------
     Start states hang off .hp-mm--reveal, which the script removes if anything
     goes wrong, so a failure shows the finished section rather than an empty
     one. */
  .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__back,
  .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__photo,
  .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__outline,
  .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__sticker,
  .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__quote,
  .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__bio {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  @keyframes hp-mm-back-in {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.9); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: scale(1); }
  }

  @keyframes hp-mm-rise {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* Ends on the sticker's own tilt, so the overshoot settles into the angle
     the merchant set rather than back to zero. */
  @keyframes hp-mm-sticker-in {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: rotate(0deg) scale(0.8); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: rotate(var(--hp-mm-rot, 0deg)) scale(1); }
  }

  .hp-mm--reveal.is-in .hp-mm__back {
    animation: hp-mm-back-in 600ms cubic-bezier(.34, 1.56, .64, 1) both;
  }

  .hp-mm--reveal.is-in .hp-mm__photo,
  .hp-mm--reveal.is-in .hp-mm__outline {
    animation: hp-mm-rise 500ms ease-out 120ms both;
  }

  .hp-mm--reveal.is-in .hp-mm__quote {
    animation: hp-mm-rise 500ms ease-out 180ms both;
  }

  .hp-mm--reveal.is-in .hp-mm__bio {
    animation: hp-mm-rise 500ms ease-out 280ms both;
  }

  .hp-mm--reveal.is-in .hp-mm__sticker {
    animation: hp-mm-sticker-in 450ms cubic-bezier(.34, 1.56, .64, 1)
               var(--hp-mm-sticker-delay, 400ms) both;
  }

  /* --- Idle wobble --------------------------------------------------------
     On the inner svg, not on .hp-mm__back: the entrance scale already owns
     that element's transform, and a second animation on the same property
     would replace it outright rather than compose with it. */
  @keyframes hp-mm-wobble {
    0%, 100% { transform: rotate(-3deg); }
    50%      { transform: rotate(3deg); }
  }

  .hp-mm--animate .hp-mm__back svg {
    animation: hp-mm-wobble 8s ease-in-out 1s infinite;
    transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  }

  /* --- Hover (pointers only) ---------------------------------------------- */
  @keyframes hp-mm-wiggle {
    0%   { transform: rotate(0deg) translateY(-2px); }
    30%  { transform: rotate(4deg) translateY(-2px); }
    70%  { transform: rotate(-4deg) translateY(-2px); }
    100% { transform: rotate(0deg) translateY(-2px); }
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .hp-mm__sticker:hover .hp-mm__pill {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      animation: hp-mm-wiggle 450ms ease-in-out;
    }

    .hp-mm__portrait:hover .hp-mm__photo img {
      transform: scale(1.04);
    }
  }

  /* --- Below 990: stack --------------------------------------------------- */
  @media screen and (max-width: 989px) {
    .hp-mm {
      padding-block: var(--hp-mm-pt-mobile) var(--hp-mm-pb-mobile);
    }

    .hp-mm__row {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 48px;
      justify-items: center;
    }

    .hp-mm__portrait { width: min(88vw, 400px); }

    .hp-mm__text {
      align-items: center;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .hp-mm__bio { max-width: 520px; }

    .hp-mm__quote { font-size: 28px; line-height: 36px; }

    /* A sticker that clears the cluster on a desktop does not clear a phone:
       the pill is a fixed number of px wide and the cluster is not. The
       right-hand presets move inboard and the pill itself gets smaller. */
    .hp-mm__pill { padding: 9px 14px; font-size: 11px; }
    .hp-mm__sticker--tr,
    .hp-mm__sticker--br { left: 56%; }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .hp-mm__quote { font-size: 22px; line-height: 30px; }
  }

  /* --- Reduced motion -----------------------------------------------------
     Everything in its final state, nothing moving. The sticker keeps its tilt
     because the tilt is the design, not the motion. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__back,
    .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__photo,
    .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__outline,
    .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__sticker,
    .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__quote,
    .hp-mm--reveal .hp-mm__bio {
      opacity: 1;
    }

    .hp-mm *,
    .hp-mm *::before,
    .hp-mm *::after {
      animation: none !important;
      transition: none !important;
    }

    .hp-mm__sticker { transform: rotate(var(--hp-mm-rot, 0deg)); }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<div
  class="hp-mm{% if animate %} hp-mm--reveal hp-mm--animate{% endif %}"
  style="
    --hp-mm-bg: {{ s.background | default: '#FCF9F4' }};
    --hp-mm-blob: {{ s.blob_color | default: '#F0C4A8' }};
    --hp-mm-ink: {{ s.ink_color | default: '#2F3427' }};
    --hp-mm-accent: {{ s.accent_color | default: '#E06E4C' }};
    --hp-mm-muted: {{ s.bio_color | default: '#5E6152' }};
    --hp-mm-placeholder: {{ s.placeholder_color | default: '#DDD6CB' }};
    --hp-mm-eyebrow-bg: {{ s.eyebrow_background | default: '#FFFFFF' }};
    --hp-mm-signature: {{ s.signature_font | default: 'Fredoka, "Chubbo", "Quicksand", ui-rounded, system-ui, sans-serif' | escape }};
    --hp-mm-pt: {{ s.padding_top | default: 140 }}px;
    --hp-mm-pb: {{ s.padding_bottom | default: 150 }}px;
    --hp-mm-pt-mobile: {{ s.padding_top_mobile | default: 80 }}px;
    --hp-mm-pb-mobile: {{ s.padding_bottom_mobile | default: 96 }}px;
  "
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <hp-mm-reveal class="hp-mm__row">
    <div class="hp-mm__portrait">
      {%- comment -%}
        The clipPath is defined once, here, in a zero-sized SVG. The id carries
        the section id: two of these on one page would otherwise share a path
        and the first defined would win for both.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <svg width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="position:absolute">
        <defs>
          <clipPath id="{{ clip_id }}" clipPathUnits="objectBoundingBox">
            <path transform="scale(0.01)" d="{{ photo_d }}"></path>
          </clipPath>
        </defs>
      </svg>

      <div class="hp-mm__back">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path d="{{ back_d }}" fill="var(--hp-mm-blob)"></path>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <div class="hp-mm__photo">
        {%- if s.portrait != blank -%}
          {{
            s.portrait
            | image_url: width: 840
            | image_tag:
              loading: portrait_loading,
              widths: '420, 640, 840',
              sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 420px, 88vw',
              alt: portrait_alt,
              class: 'hp-mm__img'
          }}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          No placeholder graphic with no photo set. Shopify's own would paint
          its illustration over the whole crop and hide the placeholder
          colour; leaving the box empty lets that colour fill the blob, so
          the shape is what shows both before a photo is chosen and while one
          is still loading.
        {%- endcomment -%}
      </div>

      <div class="hp-mm__outline">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path
            d="{{ photo_d }}"
            fill="none"
            stroke="var(--hp-mm-ink)"
            stroke-width="2"
            vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"
          ></path>
        </svg>
      </div>

      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign b = block.settings
          assign pos = b.position | default: 'tr'
          assign rot = b.rotation | default: 0
          # Stickers land after everything else, one behind the next.
          assign delay = forloop.index0 | times: 140 | plus: 400
        -%}
        {%- if b.text != blank -%}
          <div
            class="hp-mm__sticker hp-mm__sticker--{{ pos }}"
            style="
              --hp-mm-rot: {{ rot }}deg;
              --hp-mm-sticker-bg: {{ b.background | default: '#FFFFFF' | escape }};
              --hp-mm-sticker-delay: {{ delay }}ms;
            "
            {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
          >
            <span class="hp-mm__pill">{{ b.text }}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    <div class="hp-mm__text">
      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="hp-mm__eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.quote != blank -%}
        <blockquote class="hp-mm__quote">{{ s.quote }}</blockquote>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.bio != blank -%}
        <div class="hp-mm__bio">{{ s.bio }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if sig_name != blank or s.signature_title != blank -%}
        <p class="hp-mm__sig">
          {%- if sig_name != blank -%}
            <span class="hp-mm__sig-name">{{ sig_name }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.signature_title != blank -%}
            <span class="hp-mm__sig-title">{{ s.signature_title }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </hp-mm-reveal>
</div>

<script>
  (function () {
    if (customElements.get('hp-mm-reveal')) return;

    customElements.define('hp-mm-reveal', class extends HTMLElement {
      connectedCallback() {
        // Anything unexpected in here ends with the section on screen, never
        // with it stuck at opacity 0.
        try {
          this.root = this.closest('.hp-mm');
          if (!this.root || !this.root.classList.contains('hp-mm--reveal')) return;
          if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window)) return this.revealAll();
          if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;

          this.observer = new IntersectionObserver(this.onIntersect.bind(this), {
            rootMargin: '0px 0px -10% 0px',
            threshold: 0
          });
          this.observer.observe(this);
        } catch (e) {
          this.revealAll();
        }
      }

      // The theme editor tears a section down and rebuilds it on every change,
      // so the observer has to go with it.
      disconnectedCallback() {
        if (this.observer) this.observer.disconnect();
      }

      onIntersect(entries) {
        var self = this;
        entries.forEach(function (entry) {
          if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;
          self.root.classList.add('is-in');
          if (self.observer) self.observer.unobserve(self);
        });
      }

      // The class the hidden start state hangs off, so dropping it cannot
      // leave anything invisible.
      revealAll() {
        if (this.root) this.root.classList.remove('hp-mm--reveal');
      }
    });
  })();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Meet the maker",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "hp-meet-the-maker-section",
  "max_blocks": 3,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Portrait" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "portrait", "label": "Portrait image" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "portrait_alt",
      "label": "Portrait alt text",
      "info": "Describes the photo for screen readers and for anyone the image fails to load for. Falls back to the signature name."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "portrait_loading",
      "label": "When to load the portrait",
      "options": [
        { "value": "lazy", "label": "On approach — for a section partway down the page" },
        { "value": "eager", "label": "With the page — for a section near the top" }
      ],
      "default": "lazy",
      "info": "Leave this on \"on approach\" unless this section is the first thing on the page. A lazy image that is already in view is fetched late, which shows as an empty box while it loads."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Text" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Meet the maker" },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "quote",
      "label": "Quote",
      "default": "“I wanted something she’d reach for herself — not something I had to chase her with.”"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "bio",
      "label": "Bio",
      "default": "<p>Totterful is a one-mom studio with a design background and a very honest product tester at home. Every Pal starts as a sketch, gets made by hand, and only ships once it has survived a full week of real toddler life.</p>"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "signature_name", "label": "Signature name", "default": "Niku" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "signature_title", "label": "Signature title", "default": "Founder, Totterful" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Colours" },
